<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:06Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>French presidential candidate Glucksmann says 'battle begins' to unite fragmented left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e440981ffa6549bdbfaa8654bb0b715217618319027d13d4cc4b21108cc6db3</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:07:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-french-presidential-candidate-glucksmann-says-battle-begins-to-unite-fragmented-left--59d3b747ae6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-french-presidential-candidate-glucksmann-says-battle-begins-to-unite-fragmented-left" /><summary type="html">French presidential candidate Raphaël Glucksmann said Monday that the "battle begins" to revive the country's divided left ahead of the 2027 election. The EU lawmaker was elected Sunday as the centre-left candidate with more than 66 percent of the vote.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Fire destroys historic covered food market in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07631ac7c7319aef3b521df71bc3c1a2d944d2a609e0f6d70be6b3daed0c18bf</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-fire-destroys-historic-covered-food-market-in-paris--e9a2dc436f25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-fire-destroys-historic-covered-food-market-in-paris" /><summary type="html">The iconic Marché des Enfants-Rouges in Paris was ravaged by fire overnight. Adored by locals and tourists alike, it was believed to be the oldest food market in Paris. There were no casualties, but the market’s vendors have lost everything, and the history is irreplaceable. Details by Charli James.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e061501e81c628634b1180c8d2ec102b62af4b1bdc1fbd428ebb4ec796e718a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia extends Riyadh aiport suspension, vows deadly response to Houthis strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf07710d326a3448d65a508c80320662082842cac8d46d75deecb977d22fb26c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:21:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes--faba784fd28a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia extended on Monday the closure of the international airport in Riyadh after announcing the Saudi-led coalition was responding to Houthi combined drone and missile attacks. On Saturday, another attack left 13 dead and over 300 injured. This is one of the worst disruptions to Saudi aviation in years – marking a significant escalation in the war with Yemen's Houthi rebels. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chinese cars vs Europe: Who will win the battle for the market?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:491b18e26b751ca7caffcc2a9e2ea26332e9c857b373bc26484179b8adc1e4f8</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:20:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/chinese-cars-vs-europe-who-will-win-the-battle-for-the-market--488a396b2ae3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-cars-vs-europe-who-will-win-the-battle-for-the-market" /><summary type="html">The biennial Paris Motor Show officially opened this Monday in France. Over 200 auto sector brands will be present, rivalling for attention with their latest models and innovations. This competition for attention mirrors the competition for market share. This is especially true between local European brands and Chinese ones which have seen their sales surge on the continent over the past ten years – prompting accusations of unfair competition. Report by Charles Pellegrin, FRANCE 24’s business editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>The revival of a classic: Citroën unveils new electric version of its 2CV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94c2f00f179a8651cf5d1a8269e8e7f0750d0f69f42ed8e11b1c862da4d81f0a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:08:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-the-revival-of-a-classic-citro_n-unveils-new-electric-version-of-its-2cv--4f85fd5fec58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-the-revival-of-a-classic-citro%C3%ABn-unveils-new-electric-version-of-its-2cv" /><summary type="html">French car manufacturer Citroën has unveiled a new electric version of its classic 2CV. Although still a concept vehicle, the company says it plans to put the car into production within the next two years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Turning Point and the battle for Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b658381dbe01e0216aa75a63030c105b805a0d74c2609a10ba64785bfe6be26</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:59:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-midterms-2026-turning-point-and-the-battle-for-charlie-kirk-s-legacy--d6085c6fb972.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-midterms-2026-turning-point-and-the-battle-for-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">In the year following the death of Charlie Kirk, the number of American universities with Turning Point chapters surged by 64 percent. But at the same time there have been signs of division in the organisation Kirk founded and the MAGA movement more generally: far-right figures are vying for Kirk’s legacy, while conspiracy theories circulate regarding his death. But as the midterms approach, how do activists on the ground see the future of the conservative youth movement? And who, if anyone, can take on Kirk’s mantle? France 24 travelled to the place Turning Point was founded - Phoenix, Arizona - to find out more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Adieu aux ‘Enfants Rouges’: Tears and shock as fire destroys Paris’s oldest covered food market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b6c345184e44a448419e4a498b3d483a50f1ca921cf6b7e998ae079544557a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:28:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-adieu-aux-enfants-rouges-tears-shock-fire-destroys-paris-oldest-covered-food-market--54f82012bcab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261012-adieu-aux-enfants-rouges-tears-shock-fire-destroys-paris-oldest-covered-food-market" /><summary type="html">A devastating blaze destroyed the French capital’s oldest covered food market in the early hours of Monday, stripping Paris of a cherished venue popular with locals and tourists alike. Traders and residents said the destruction of the Enfants Rouges market, named after a 16th-century orphanage, had left them feeling “orphaned” themselves.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>India's opposition leader marches with thousands against election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0531ee9297c3aada4b4892d696c24f43e19e6e7c9bd678b39a2b0a69a5fa4f4c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:14:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief--11dd429412fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties and supporters of the so-called "cockroach" youth movement marched towards the country's Supreme Court on Monday, in the latest show of outrage against the recent removal of millions of names from voters lists. Critics say the move is likely to benefit Prime Minister Narendra Modi's ruling party – and are demanding India's election chief step down over what they describe as misconduct. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in New Delhi, Navodita Kumari.</summary></entry><entry><title>US federal agents raid home of Democratic congresswoman and Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b099123c3ecd20f12611d5d7327ebc0a3be9cf0b789180c75eb512f74efcde25</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:13:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar--1078c3e6f713.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar" /><summary type="html">US federal agents on Monday launched a raid on ‌the Washington home of Democratic representative Ilhan Omar, an outspoken critic of US President Donald ⁠Trump, officials said. The raid followed a criminal fraud ‌investigation into the Somali-born lawmaker's immigration paperwork submitted by her late father when she ⁠was a child, Fox News reported.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Five people missing as fresh flash floods hit central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8db2631c325e0cdbcd9d8f765aa1923175b24b88384cfc53c07012a94b3250e5</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal--2d9a2373d2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Nepali rescuers searched for five missing people on Monday, a day after new flash floods swept away more than 200 houses and five bridges along the Budhi Gandaki River. The country is still recovering from devastating floods, triggered by a mountain glacial collapse on August 26, which killed more than 1,400 people and left over 5,000 missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>2026 Paris Motor Show: Western carmakers face steep competition from Chinese rivals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f432ceba1d4d88fd4b7bb5f93bfead1c4be405fd09dd1e745030dcebdb0b919c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:30:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261012-2026-paris-motor-show-western-carmakers-face-steep-competition-from-chinese-rivals--0af43bfd0c7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261012-2026-paris-motor-show-western-carmakers-face-steep-competition-from-chinese-rivals" /><summary type="html">The Paris Motor Show roars into gear this Monday, with over 200 auto sector brands showcasing their latest models and innovations. Chinese brands like BYD, Xpeng and Zeekr are among those present and getting lots of attention as their market share has surged in the past few years. In this edition, we speak to John Bozzella, CEO of the Alliance for Automotive Innovation, about the challenge these new competitors represent for the European and North American auto sectors.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>SARAB pay homage to war victims in Syria, Gaza on new album</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85bd7f62a30a5b4a4460b0f0064dd52df171a866a0f6b15c5e69467445c5d94d</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:24:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261012-sarab-pay-homage-to-war-victims-in-syria-gaza-on-new-album--b0e270000038.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261012-sarab-pay-homage-to-war-victims-in-syria-gaza-on-new-album" /><summary type="html">Franco-Syrian five-piece SARAB, or mirage in Arabic, make what can be described as poetic punk rock, blending guitar-heavy riffs with classical Arabic sounds and socially conscious lyrics. They're on tour with their latest album "Mit Warde – Cent Roses", a record dedicated to the victims of war around the world, from Gaza to Syria. We also speak to Tom McFarland from British neo-soul band Jungle, who are on tour with their radiant fifth album "Sunshine".</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d8287f1f18960407dc89a19c64461d77da234fe88aeb443d65810b3cffa295d</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-_600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe--6b8c747aa05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe" /><summary type="html">The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months, and countries must claim and account for the remaining funds.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be758b5e65cb765f4090a11ff14c971720811185c08c2de7bf3f60847502f304</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:05:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon--559bc068ffcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Concerts of pro-Assad singers cancelled in Syria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cf8570b7a59e8362d37d4ae69f63a9200d45a018c7d72aa1d6d2429510e9c21</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:53:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261012-concerts-pro-assad-singers-cancelled--7f221a636658.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261012-concerts-pro-assad-singers-cancelled" /><summary type="html">The concerts of several singers accused of supporting the regime of deposed president Bashar al-Assad have been cancelled this summer in Syria. People in Homs ripped down posters advertising performances by artists Mohamad Iskandar and Hossam Jneed, denouncing their previous links with the regime. One of the musicians later publicly apologised.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Old jeans could shield your home from the next heatwave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9f4cc5b4b015c6219bc73e7c6c5f591e34b2f2d15e70deb8ca0f261608f7cd0</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:42:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261012-old-jeans-could-shield-your-home-from-the-next-heatwave--796fd5582d72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261012-old-jeans-could-shield-your-home-from-the-next-heatwave" /><summary type="html">We all have that one pair of old jeans in the back of our wardrobe – don’t throw them out! A French company says denim fibres make for great insulation against the cold and heat. Millions of jeans are already being recycled in a factory in north of the country. Their insulating panels have even found their way into some of France's most iconic buildings. Our Down to Earth team reports.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Capital punishment in US: Elected judges, prosecutors seek 'results', 'not interested in the truth'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9f775543bae1444d9701cb9cfc994f9501126a60a7e8b83193868f26a8e85d7</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:27:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-trut--c9271d966485.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-truth" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, author, advocate against the death penalty and member of the association "Ensemble contre la peine de mort": Together Against the Death Penalty. She asserts that capital punishment is “really a political agenda, especially in electoral times.”</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'Perfect Victims' author Mohammed El-Kurd challenges how Palestinian suffering is viewed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fd6ef754119490e47f94499022c348ecc82bb4056e6d653425b7c532d8e7eaf</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:12:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261012-perfect-victims-author-mohammed-el-kurd-challenges-how-palestinian-suffering-is-viewed--ba6b4c5c0ead.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261012-perfect-victims-author-mohammed-el-kurd-challenges-how-palestinian-suffering-is-viewed" /><summary type="html">Mohammed El-Kurd is a Palestinian writer, poet and journalist. He is the author of the poetry collection Rifqa and the book "Perfect Victims and the Politics of Appeal", which was just published in French translation last week. Mohammed grew up in Sheikh Jarrah in East Jerusalem and as a child, his family were displaced from their home by Israeli settlers in a high-profile eviction. He spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:722d1c8ad16ad80b235b268dd0d4ba136814ac263a407ab7aec1c3c1d7c3167a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:41:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile--6a6b5384d4d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile" /><summary type="html">NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58a2ae807f31740f3471ab9130ada0a13c834fd83269643d7c2dd0cb75db9026</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:26:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage--36373f6834b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage" /><summary type="html">And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae685303d0496be3d93f55767c074c09b2c45338716f47e8a4fecd8b1b51f234</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:24:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media--eb569c8092c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media" /><summary type="html">An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.</summary></entry><entry><title>Citroën bets on nostalgia at Paris motor show amid struggling French sales</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f40fe457b19ab8f40a43c1a262795e5d150f026cdf4349f9bccfb443266bd4</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-citro_n-bets-on-nostalgia-at-paris-motor-show-amis-struggling-french-sales--f270d8610893.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-citro%C3%ABn-bets-on-nostalgia-at-paris-motor-show-amis-struggling-french-sales" /><summary type="html">French president Emmanuel Macron is paying his customary visit to the Paris Motor Show this morning. This year's show sees electric and hybrid vehicles in the spotlight as European carbuilders seek to roll back years of sliding sales. The sector has been given a boost by China's commitment to stem the flow of Chinese e-vehicles, and some builders, such as the multinational Stellantis are betting on small affordable electric cars to win back customers. And one of the models it has lined up is an electric reboot of a French classic: the Citroën 2CV. FRANCE 24’s Charles Pellegrin interviewed Citroen CEO Xavier Chardon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Striking images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cea7b7115a5a5c8459f9473ee7c3970951931c7f270b26b637d07ee03240e62b</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:14:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal--99e18aa6713c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Striking new images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal. This comes only six weeks after another disaster there left more than 1,400 dead and 5,000 missing. According to an initial assessment by the Nepalese authorities, at least five people are now missing. Elitsa Gadeva and France 2 have the details.</summary></entry></feed>
